    64	
    65	- `SessionStore.lookup?(sessionId)` is optional: a store with only the five original members still satisfies the interface, beside the shipped one that has it ([validated by: leaves a store with only the five original members satisfying the interface beside the shipped one](../../src/infrastructure/stores/sessionStoreLookupSignature.test.ts#L39)).
    66	- It is named `lookup`, not `load`, so a durable store's own `load` of another shape still compiles beside it ([validated by: compiles beside a store's own load method of a different shape](../../src/infrastructure/stores/sessionStoreLookupSignature.test.ts#L48)).
    67	- `InMemorySessionStore.lookup` reports a session past `maxAgeMs` as `{status: 'expired', userId}`, with no `session` ([validated by: reports a session past maxAgeMs as expired, with its owner and nothing else](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemorySessionLookup.test.ts#L20)).
